# Scraped pages and everything derived from them. This line is the DEFAULT, not
# the guard: `git add -f` defeats it, and once a file is tracked `git
# check-ignore` stops reporting it at all, because a tracked file is never
# "ignored". The guard is
# tests/unit/tools/scraped-output-is-never-committed.test.ts, which asks
# `git ls-files` what is actually tracked.
scraped/
.tmp/
tools/discord-launcher/.env
__pycache__/
.vtt-soak-out/
.tmp-*
dnd-slim-runs/

# Licensing wall (D369 era): BG3-derived notes must never be committed to this public repo
docs/design/bg3-*.md

# Art delivered by the image-generation assistant (the responses to art/requests)
# is a scratch channel too (D628): never tracked, README included. The canonical
# folder for final art is public/assets/art/ (tracked, licence CC0, inventory pinned).
art/incoming/

# Art requests are a scratch channel between the Ubuntu-side assistant and the
# Windows-side image assistant (D628): never tracked. Final art is committed
# only when promoted into public/assets/art/.
art/requests/
